    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30953" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nī^gror</span></b> , ōris,
			m.
		1. niger, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>blackness</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in
			post-Aug. prose): noctis, Pac. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Div.
				1, 14, 24</span></i>; Lucil. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 515,
			5</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mortis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					3, 39</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nigrorem in ulceribus excitat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 2,
					1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rubidus est rufus, atrore et nigrore multo
					mixtus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 2, 26, 14</span></i>
			.</div>
